# NOTE: processes_pdf/ and Workflows/ are deliberately TRACKED for now, so the
# deduplicated corpus survives a clone and the workflow extraction can be run
# on a machine with the vision model pulled. Once that has happened they go
# back to being local-only and these two lines come back:
#   processes_pdf/
#   Workflows/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated on every run. Each line names the command that writes it.
#
# What is NOT here, and why: chunks.json, workflow_chunks.json and the two
# workflow_audit_*.json files are also rewritten on every run, but they stay
# tracked on purpose. They are the artifacts a clone needs in order to answer
# questions without re-running 133 vision-model calls, and workflow_audit_full
# .json is the input `--from-audit` re-renders from. They are outputs that are
# also inputs; everything below is only an output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# python extract_pipeline.py   (OCR-health audit; rewritten whole each run)
files/extracted_raw.json
files/ocr_fallback_log.json

# demo_chatbot.ipynb §1 on every Run All — the notebook's own copies of the above
files/demo_extracted_raw.json
files/demo_ocr_fallback_log.json

# streamlit run app.py — session log, append-only, grows without bound
files/streamlit_log.txt

# one-off single-document re-extractions, named after the PDF
files/rerun_*.json

# default output paths of the --audit / --json flags, for throwaway runs:
#   python adaptive_chunker.py --audit audit.json
#   python document_router.py --json routing.json
files/audit.json
files/routing.json
audit.json
routing.json
